        {
         "insert": "Simple Lehengas"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "list": "bullet"
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "\n\nWhat Are The Latest Wedding Lehenga Designs For This Wedding Season?"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "header": 2
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "With the wedding season in full swing, brides-to-be are on the hunt for the perfect lehenga to dazzle on their special day. This year, trends are moving beyond the traditional red and embracing an array of colours, from blush pink and mint green to bold royal blue. Minimal bridal lehenga-new design is also taking centre stage, with intricate threadwork and subtle embellishments replacing heavy embroidery. The A-line dulhan lehenga design remains a popular choice for a flattering silhouette, while the lehenga-saree fusion offers a unique and unconventional twist. And for the eco-conscious bride, sustainable fabrics like organic silk and khadi are making a statement. Remember, the most important thing is to choose a lehenga that makes you feel confident and radiantly beautiful – after all, it's your day to shine! \n"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "header": 2
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "Which Colour Is Trending Now In Bridal Lehenga?"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "header": 2
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "Certain colours including red, yellow and maroon are considered auspicious and Indian brides have been donning these colours for the longest time. However, modern brides are experimenting with unique colours and trends like pastel colours and muted tones. While keeping the trends in mind is a good thing, be sure that you aren’t following trends blindly while choosing your bridal lehenga. Weddings By Betterhalf’s Ideabook with the most exquisite bridal lehenga collection features lehengas in all colours and trends for you to choose the best ones.\n"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "header": 2
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "How Much Do Wedding Lehengas Cost?"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "header": 2
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "The cost incurred in your bridal lehenga depends on several factors. To start with, the fabric used to create the lehenga and the intricacy of the work decides the price of the lehenga. Further, the designer label matters a lot regarding your lehenga’s cost. In India, you can get a bridal lehenga for as little as ₹15,000 from a local market, and the prices can go up to ₹8,00,000- ₹10,00,000 depending on the designer. Explore the Indian fashion market with bridal lehenga at prices, and pick your favourite lehengas to make your special day even more special. \n"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "header": 2
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "Latest Bridal Lehenga Trends of Indian Wedding"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "header": 2
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "The trending bridal lehengas in our ideabook blend traditional charm with modern styles, making them perfect for women on their wedding day. Whether you're the bride (dulhan) looking for the ideal lehenga for wedding or just a fan of wedding fashion, these Indian wedding lehengas are designed to stand out. They feature beautiful fabrics and detailed embroidery, telling a story of elegance and glamour. Explore these stylish wedding lehengas to ensure you look stunning and shine on your special day. Choose the most popular and sought-after wedding lehenga for women, adding a touch of classic beauty and contemporary flair to your bridal look.\n"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "header": 2
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "How soon should you start shopping for Bridal Lehengas?"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "header": 2
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "Ideally, 6 to 9 months. \n\nYour wedding is a once-in-lifetime event and you got to look perfect on this special day. You must start looking for your options at least 6-9 months before the wedding day. This can be done by keeping an eye on bridal fashion shows, visiting designer stores, and browsing the latest bridal lehnga for wedding trends in Weddings By Betterhalf’s ideabook. 4-6 months before your wedding is the time when you must have a narrowed-down list of options for your bridal couture. 2-3 months before your wedding is the time to decide on your ultimate lehenga for wedding. The stitching of your lehenga must be done a month before your wedding. Remember to try your outfit a week before your wedding to make sure it fits. \n"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "header": 2
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "Who is the famous Bridal lehenga designer?"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "header": 2
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "There are several renowned bridal lehenga designers in India, each known for their unique styles and contributions to the world of bridal fashion. Some of the most popular names include Sabyasachi Mukherjee, Manish Malhotra, Tarun Tahiliani, Anita Dongre, Abu Jani Sandeep Khosla, Ritu Kumar, and many more. \n"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "header": 2
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "How to Choose the Perfect Bridal Lehenga"
        },
        {
         "attributes": {
          "header": 2
         },
         "insert": "\n"
        },
        {
         "insert": "A beautiful bridal lehenga is a blend of personal style, comfort, and cultural aesthetics. Starting the search early allows for a thoughtful exploration of various designs and styles. Setting a budget is key, ensuring that the dream lehenga aligns with financial considerations. Consider your body type and opt for a silhouette that enhances your natural beauty. The choice of fabric, whether silk, velvet, or georgette, should harmonize with the wedding season. While traditional reds and maroons are timeless, contemporary brides are embracing a spectrum of colours, letting personal preferences and the overall theme guide their choice. \n\nComfort is paramount for a day filled with festivities, and a trial is essential to assess fit and movement. Trusting your instincts in the selection process ensures that the chosen bridal lehenga not only complements the celebration's aesthetics but also becomes a cherished reflection of your unique style and the joy of the occasion.\n"
        }
       ]
      }
